  "coverage": [
    "Stable checkpoint projections carry nonserialized provenance only for affected rows. Reconciliation uses deterministic persisted views and retained mappings without reopening archives. Missing/unsafe archives produce historical uncertainty while genuine external edits still conflict.",
    "Filesystem-independent portable normalization and fallback IDs precede checkpoint projection. Read-only load/export, stored IDs and provider replay associations remain unchanged.",
    "Normal agent turns and selective appends persist older normalized checkpoint rows and references transactionally before relocation, resume, fork and compaction. Audit triggers verify one pending row update and no repeated updates or archive opens.",
    "Owning and nested writes, external nested commits, rollback, deferred commit failure, full replacement, multiple snapshots and the next write before reload retain correct provenance. Source fingerprints prevent overwriting external changes; post-commit acknowledgement is allocation-free.",
    "StateStore shares its injected filesystem with Tools in production. Tests inject normalization, backup, fork and receipt failures. Lazy artifact anchors tolerate unavailability for database operations, retry failed acquisition and reject replacement after pinning.",
    "Per-preparation repeated references validate once. Changed checkpoint preparation permits another connection to commit before the writer lock; publication of pending mappings performs no archive opens.",
    "Revision repair relies on verified delete triggers for nonempty histories and explicitly rotates tokens when deleting zero provider rows. Existing malformed-token, strict infrastructure, backup, commit/rollback and operational-error tests remain passing.",
    "Fault controls reset at fixture and case boundaries without destroying observations needed for assertions. The complete fault suite passes twenty shuffled repetitions.",
    "Semgrep fixtures reject filesystem-dependent normalization in reconciliation and direct native filesystem construction in consolidated persistence operations. Existing provider cache, streaming and repair safeguards remain in force.",
    "Full offline host, sanitizer and Linux suites, analyzers/detection/runner checks, pinned Semgrep, benchmarks and Tiger cross-build/static checks identify executed tests separately from non-executed target hardware verification.",
    "Interleaved large provider histories retain suffix-only persistence and zero unchanged-row reads; serialized cache caps, capture quotas and zero ordinary capture scans remain intact."
  ],
